    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d786">

                <pb facs="0883" n="873" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg873"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.0015/11–448: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-11-04T17:00:00-05:00">November 4, 1948—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1548. Dept has refrained from representing to Navy desirability of following
                    course of action such as recommended by Clubb (Peiping’s tel to Nanking 609, Oct
                        29<anchor n="40" xml:id="d786-f1"/>) pending receipt statement from Emb
                    action taken locally.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d786-f1" n="40" xml:id="d786-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to the Department as telegram No. 410, <ref target="#pg869">p.
                    869</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
